Premise: 

You hold items are still "unresolved" and settle them later, most recent first (Last in first out)

Main patterns:

- Matching/Nesting (Push openers and pop when the closer arrives)
- Keep the stack increasing/decreasing. Popping an element means you found the next greatest/smallest
- Undo/Collapse (The next item can cancel or merge with the top)

How to recognize: 

- "Next/previous smaller/greater element" or "How far until something bigger/smaller" 
- Each element's answer depends on the nearest element that blocks it 
- A brute force of looping is O(n2)

How not to recognize: 

- You need the oldest element first
- You need the largest/smallest overall (Heap)
- Isn't about 'nearest' - any pair works (hashmap or two pointers)
- Sorted input with pair conditions 